1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,037
Four and a half thousand years ago, while Egypt built its pyramids,

2
00:00:05,037 --> 00:00:08,700
a city on the Indus had drains under every street.

3
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:10,275
This is Mohenjo-daro.

4
00:00:10,275 --> 00:00:15,100
With Harappa, it was the heart of the Indus Valley Civilisation.

5
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,662
Streets ran in a grid.

6
00:00:16,662 --> 00:00:19,552
Bricks were baked to the same proportions.

7
00:00:19,552 --> 00:00:22,100
Most homes had their own bathroom.

8
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,662
Merchants stamped their goods with seals,

9
00:00:24,662 --> 00:00:27,500
in a script no one can read, to this day.

10
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:30,490
Around 1900 BCE, the rivers shifted,

11
00:00:30,490 --> 00:00:34,500
the monsoon weakened, and the cities emptied.

12
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:40,437
Four thousand years later, archaeologists dug into a mound called Mohenjo-daro.

13
00:00:40,437 --> 00:00:42,662
The Mound of the Dead.
